<title>USA: Fed seen refraining from open market operations.</title>
<headline>Fed seen refraining from open market operations.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve Bank of New York is expected to refrain from open market operations on Friday, analysts said.</p>
<p>&quot;We expect no Fed today,&quot; said an economist at consulting firm Stone &amp; McCarthy Research Associates Inc.</p>
<p>Analysts at MMS International Inc consultants also see the central bank refraining from open market deals.</p>
<p>At 1100 EDT/1500 GMT, fed funds were trading at 5-1/4 percent, in line with the Fed's target.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk 212-859-1660</p>
